  "text": "alex: CI failed on PR #1012 while building the docs site. Two problems: some images in `getting-started` are 404ing (looks like srcset urls went bad after static move) and there's an MDX parse warning about an unclosed HTML comment. Anyone on images today?\n\ndocs-ci-bot: build failed: mkdocs build exit code 1\nlog excerpt: \"Linkcheck: /docs/getting-started#architecture-diagram -> 404\"\nlog excerpt: \"MDX parse warning: Unexpected EOF while in HTML comment at docs/getting-started/overview.mdx:58\"\n\nmira: I moved a bunch of diagrams to `docs/static/images/diagrams` in the PR to centralize assets. I also updated some examples to use `srcset` to serve hi-dpi images. Example line from overview.mdx: \n```mdx\n![arch](../static/images/diagrams/arch.png \"arch\")\n<img srcset=\"../static/images/diagrams/arch@2x.png 2x, ../static/images/diagrams/arch.png 1x\" src=\"../static/images/diagrams/arch.png\" />\n<!-- TODO: remove temp note\n```\nThat trailing comment open is my bad \u2014 I forgot to close it.\n\nsam: the srcset paths look fine relatively, but our deploy preview rewrites static assets with a CDN prefix. If any path has an extra `../` or a stray space, the CDN normalizer may break the redirect. Also some hosting layers strip `title` or `<title>` from inline svgs which used to provide anchor ids. Do we reference the diagram via `#architecture-diagram` anchor?\n\nalex: yes, overview.mdx had an internal link from tutorials/setup: `[see architecture](../getting-started/overview#architecture-diagram)` and the anchor used to be provided by an SVG `<title>Architecture diagram</title>` inlined in the page. After the SVG optimizer removed `<title>` the anchor vanished.\n\ntony: quick fixes:\n- close the HTML comment (MDX error)\n- prefer adding an explicit wrapping id: `<div id=\"architecture-diagram\">` around the inline svg or example component so anchors don't rely on svg titles\n- normalize srcset paths to use `/static/images/...` (rooted) so CDN rewrite is stable across preview and prod\n- add a GH Action `docs/mdx-lint` to catch unclosed HTML comments and a small `docs/srcset-verify` script that checks each `srcset` entry exists (and no trailing spaces)\n\nmira: on it. I can patch the PR with: close comment, add wrapper div with id, and convert `srcset` to root paths. Commit msg: \"docs(images): fix mdx comment, add wrapper id for diagram, normalize srcset paths\".\n\ndocs-ci-bot: CI: rebuild triggered for PR #1012 (branch: fix/docs-images-srcset)\ndocs-ci-bot: build failed: mkdocs build exit code 1\nlog excerpt: \"Linkcheck: /docs/getting-started#architecture-diagram -> 404\"\n\nsam: still failing for linkcheck? Did the wrapper id land in the right file and in the built HTML? Sometimes MDX compiles JSX fragments into different wrappers so the `id` can move. We should check the generated HTML in the preview artifacts.\n\nmira: oh \u2014 I pushed the wrapper but used `id=\"architecture-diagram \"` (accidental trailing space)  which makes the id invalid and linkcheck can't match. Fixing and repushing.\n\nalex: oof trailing-space-in-id \u2014 classic. Maybe we should add a tiny grep in the docs lint that flags `id=\".*\\s+\"` or trailing spaces in attributes.\n\ntony: agreed. I'll author a small action that runs a few quick sanity checks on PRs touching `docs/**`:\n- yamllint for frontmatter\n- mdx-lint for unclosed comments and stray raw HTML\n- a quick regex pass for `srcset` entries that end with spaces and for `id=\".*\\s+\"`\nIt should be fast and non-blocking at first (comment-only), then we can promote to required.\n\ndocs-ci-bot: CI: rebuild triggered for PR #1012 (branch: fix/docs-images-srcset-v2)\ndocs-ci-bot: build succeeded, preview deployed -> https://deploy-preview-1012.docs.redwood.com/getting-started/overview#architecture-diagram\n\nsam: preview shows the anchor resolving now and the `srcset` resources load via CDN. No mdx warnings.\n\nmira: thanks for the catch on the trailing space \u2014 pushing a follow-up PR to add the `srcset-verify` unit script and to update CONTRIBUTING with a note: \"Prefer root `/static/...` paths in srcset and avoid relying on SVG <title> for anchors\".\n\nalex: and please add the mdx-lint GH Action as `docs/mdx-lint` (comment-only initially). We'll make it required after a week of running.\n\ntony: will do. I'll open the action PR and include quick tests.\n\nalex: awesome \u2014 merging the hotfix PR now. Thanks all :shipit: ",
